## Machine marker vocabulary

The readiness validator consumes these byte-exact forms:

- `RALPH-FACT: <key>: <value>` records a verified project fact.
- `RALPH-FACT: <key>: RALPH-PENDING (assumed <date>); review trigger: <cond>` records a deferred fact.
- `RALPH-COMMAND: <approved-tool …>` records a runnable gate.
- `RALPH-INAPPLICABLE: <reason>` records a gate that never applies.
- `RALPH-PENDING: <approved-tool …> (assumed <date>); review trigger: <cond>` records an applicable deferred gate.
- `RALPH-REVIEW: <procedure>; evidence: <record>; owner: <role>` records required human review.

```text
RALPH-PENDING: pytest (assumed 2026-07-12); review trigger: once test deps are installed
RALPH-FACT: secret_scan_command: RALPH-PENDING (assumed 2026-07-12); review trigger: once a scanner is chosen
```

Every `RALPH-COMMAND` begins with an approved first token. A truthful `RALPH-PENDING` entry is an explicit accepted deferral, not an unresolved placeholder. Record applicable unresolved requirements with `RALPH-PENDING` and permanently irrelevant ones with `RALPH-INAPPLICABLE`. Each applicable typecheck or lint language has `RALPH-LANG: <Language>` followed by its command, inapplicable declaration, or deferral.

